# EAS Build archive rules — must live at the GIT REPOSITORY ROOT (this repo's
# .git is here, one level above frontend/), because EAS CLI always archives
# starting from the git root, not from wherever `eas build` was run
# (https://expo.fyi/eas-build-archive). A root .easignore, once present,
# REPLACES every .gitignore in the tree for archiving purposes — it does not
# merge with them — so this file re-states frontend/.gitignore's own rules
# below rather than relying on it.
#
# Without this file, EAS was archiving the ENTIRE monorepo: backend/
# (283MB, mostly backend/.venv_test at 268MB), backtest_data/ (303MB),
# backtest/, and a pile of report PDFs/CSVs/MD files at the repo root —
# none of which the Android/iOS app needs, and together the likely cause of
# the 233MB compressed archive and the upload failing partway through.

# 1. Ignore everything at the repo root by default...
/*
# ...except the Expo app itself, which EAS actually needs to build.
!/frontend

# 2. frontend/.gitignore's own rules, restated here since this file
#    supersedes it entirely for EAS's purposes.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.expo/
frontend/dist/
frontend/web-build/
frontend/expo-env.d.ts
frontend/.metro-health-check*
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
frontend/app-example
frontend/.env*.local
frontend/*.jks
frontend/*.p8
frontend/*.p12
frontend/*.key
frontend/*.mobileprovision
frontend/*.pem

# 3. Local cache/build junk with no .gitignore entry but no business in a
#    build archive either — .metro-cache alone was ~120MB on its own.
frontend/.metro-cache/
frontend/.pytest_cache/
**/.DS_Store
**/npm-debug.*
**/yarn-debug.*
**/yarn-error.*
